# Copy to .env.local for local development.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# The trailing path matters: every backend route lives under /api/ and every
# one of them requires a trailing slash.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000/api

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TEMPORARY — phased client testing. Remove with src/domain/phase.ts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which rollout phase a build shows. Read at BUILD time, so changing it means
# a rebuild — a tester cannot flip it from the browser.
#
#   1  Inbound: master data, group and production orders, receipts
#   2  ...plus inventory adjustments and warehouse transfers
#   3  ...plus outbound: orders, picking, shipping, backorders
#
# LEAVE IT UNSET for development and for the real release: unset shows every
# phase. Set it only on a build handed to the client for a testing session.
#
#   VITE_PHASE=1 npm run build
#
# It hides work in progress. It is NOT a permission — the server knows nothing
# about phases and will answer a Phase 3 request from a Phase 1 build.
# VITE_PHASE=1
